# AI Assistant Guidelines for Day One Content Operations

**Purpose**: This file provides coding standards and best practices for AI assistants working with this Sanity Studio + Next.js monorepo.

---

## Project Context

**Tech Stack**:
- **Sanity Studio 4.15.0** - Multi-workspace CMS
- **Next.js 16.0.0** - App Router frontend
- **TypeScript 5.9.3** - Strict mode enabled
- **React 19.2.0** - UI framework
- **pnpm workspaces** - Monorepo management
- **Biome 2.3.6** - Formatting and linting

**Architecture**:
- Multi-site content management with automatic `sites` field injection
- Type generation from Studio schemas to Web frontend
- Live preview with Visual Editing
- Page builder system with modular blocks
- GROQ queries for content fetching

---

## TypeScript Rules (CRITICAL)

### 1. Never Use `any` Type
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
const handleChange = (value: any) => { ... }

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS
interface HandleChangeProps {
  value: string | number;
  fieldName: string;
}
const handleChange = ({ value, fieldName }: HandleChangeProps) => { ... }
```

### 2. Avoid Variable Shadowing
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER shadow imports
import { getSite } from './SITES';
const basePath = (getSite: string) => `/${getSite}`; // BAD: shadows import

// ✅ ALWAYS use different names
import { getSite } from './SITES';
const basePath = (siteName: string) => `/${siteName}`; // GOOD
```

### 3. Prefer Interfaces Over Types
```typescript
// ✅ For object shapes, use interfaces
interface DocumentSchema {
  name: string;
  title: string;
  fields: FieldDefinition[];
}

// ✅ Use types for unions and primitives
type SiteName = 'site-1' | 'site-2';
```

### 4. Type Assertions Require Validation
```typescript
// ❌ Unsafe type assertion
const doc = schema as DocumentDefinition;

// ✅ Type assertion with guard
const doc = schema as DocumentDefinition;
if (!doc.fields) {
  console.warn(`Schema ${doc.name} has no fields`);
  return schema;
}
```

### 5. Use Generated Types from Studio
```typescript
// ✅ Import generated types from Studio typegen
import type { HOMEPAGE_EVENTS_QUERYResult } from '@/sanity/types';

// ✅ Use Extract for discriminated unions
type HeroBlock = Extract<
  NonNullable<PAGE_QUERY_SITE_1Result['pageBuilder']>[number],
  { _type: 'hero' }
>;
```

