## Common Development Tasks

### Adding a New Document Type
1. Create schema in `apps/studio/schemaTypes/documents/newType.ts`
2. Export from `apps/studio/schemaTypes/documents/index.ts`
3. Run `cd apps/studio && pnpm typegen`
4. The `sites` field is automatically injected

### Adding a Page Builder Block
1. Create schema in `apps/studio/schemaTypes/blocks/newBlock.ts`
2. Export from `apps/studio/schemaTypes/index.ts`
3. Update GROQ query in `apps/web/src/sanity/lib/queries.ts`
4. Run `cd apps/studio && pnpm typegen`
5. Create component in `apps/web/src/app/components/blocks/newBlock.tsx`
6. Add case to `page-builder.tsx` switch statement

### Debugging Type Issues
```bash
# 1. Schema changed but types not updating?
cd apps/studio
pnpm typegen

# 2. Still having issues? Clean build
cd apps/studio
rm -rf .next dist
pnpm build

# 3. Verify types were generated
cat apps/web/src/sanity/types.ts | grep "YourQueryName"
```

---

## Code Quality Checks

### Before Committing
```bash
# Run Biome formatter and linter
pnpm biome

# Check TypeScript compilation
cd apps/studio && tsc --noEmit
cd apps/web && tsc --noEmit

# Ensure types are up to date
cd apps/studio && pnpm typegen
```

### Common Issues to Avoid
1. ❌ Variable shadowing (function names, imports, constants)
2. ❌ Using `any` type instead of proper interfaces
3. ❌ Type assertions without validation guards
4. ❌ Editing generated `types.ts` file manually
5. ❌ Forgetting to run `pnpm typegen` after schema changes
6. ❌ Mismatched PROJECT_ID between Studio and Web
7. ❌ Hardcoded values instead of using SITES configuration
8. ❌ Dead code in conditionals (e.g., `site ? 'value' : ''` when site is always truthy)

