## File Structure References

### Key Files
- `apps/studio/sanity.config.ts` - Multi-workspace configuration
- `apps/studio/schemaTypes/index.ts:10-42` - Sites field injection logic
- `apps/studio/lib/SITES.ts` - Site metadata configuration
- `apps/web/src/sanity/lib/queries.ts` - All GROQ queries
- `apps/web/src/sanity/lib/live.ts` - sanityFetch with draft mode
- `apps/web/src/sanity/types.ts` - Generated types (DO NOT EDIT)

### Common Patterns
- Schema definitions: `apps/studio/schemaTypes/documents/*.ts`
- Page builder blocks: `apps/studio/schemaTypes/blocks/*.ts`
- Structure customization: `apps/studio/structure/*.ts`
- Custom inputs: `apps/studio/schemaTypes/components/*.tsx`
- Block renderers: `apps/web/src/app/components/blocks/*.tsx`

---

## Best Practices Summary

### DO
✅ Use TypeScript interfaces for all object shapes
✅ Run `pnpm typegen` after every schema change
✅ Validate environment variables at startup
✅ Use guard clauses for early returns
✅ Keep structure patterns consistent across workspaces
✅ Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs
✅ Import generated types from `@/sanity/types`
✅ Use `groq` template tag for queries
✅ Follow the type generation workflow
✅ Run `pnpm biome` before committing

### DON'T
❌ Never use `any` type - create proper interfaces
❌ Never shadow imported functions or constants
❌ Never edit `apps/web/src/sanity/types.ts` manually
❌ Never use type assertions without validation
❌ Never hardcode site names - use SITES configuration
❌ Never commit with TypeScript errors
❌ Never skip environment variable validation
❌ Never use redundant type casts (e.g., `String()` on strings)
❌ Never write dead code in conditionals

